On the supplied 29x18 demo (0-indexed), only the color-4 component at rows 3-4, cols 7-9 changed to color 3. Its exact occupied cells were (3,7),(3,8),(3,9),(4,8),(4,9). All other cells remained unchanged, including the nearby color-4 vertical line at col 11 and separate color-4 forms at rows 12-14 and row 25. Other distractors included color-5 clusters and a long color-3 line/component.

This confirms sparse component recoloring, but a single example does not reveal the selector. In particular, proximity to the vertical color-4 line or being a non-singleton patch is insufficient evidence. On recurrence, record exact changed and unchanged components for each demo, compare their structural context across demos, and use another demonstration to discriminate explicit candidate rules before submitting. Do not guess an edit from the changed component's color, size, or isolated appearance.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u032/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/task-50a83913-first-demo-review.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/compact-output-interpretation.md", "content": "# Interpreting compact ARC outputs

When demonstrations map a larger grid to a small output, treat the output as a structured encoding rather than an arbitrary answer shape. For every demo, establish:

- what input region(s) correspond to output rows and columns;
- whether non-background markers are copied, recolored, aggregated, or filtered;
- how empty/background output cells are determined;
- whether partitions, separator lines, or repeated tiles define independent source regions.

Record the exact source-to-output mapping and check every output cell against multiple pairs. Similar output dimensions alone do not establish the encoding. Before using the rule on a test, derive the output cell-by-cell and verify dimensions. If plausible mappings disagree, use the next demo to distinguish them; do not submit a guessed uniform pattern merely to conserve attempts.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u032/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-solving/references/compact-output-interpretation.md"}
